WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.117
This model follows one real, published case.

00:00:03.467 --> 00:00:07.265
A man aged 54 had a keratocyst at the root tips of two lower left teeth.

00:00:07.615 --> 00:00:11.369
It is a sac in the jaw. It is not cancer, but it often comes back.

00:00:12.169 --> 00:00:14.124
The surgeon lifted out the whole sac,

00:00:14.124 --> 00:00:16.607
shaved the bone wall and cut off the root tips.

00:00:17.407 --> 00:00:19.007
The teeth stayed in place.

00:00:19.807 --> 00:00:22.175
A gel made from his own blood filled the space.

00:00:22.525 --> 00:00:26.151
Three years later the bone had healed, and the cyst had not come back.

00:00:26.951 --> 00:00:28.922
There are several ways to treat a keratocyst,

00:00:28.922 --> 00:00:31.069
and how often it comes back differs between them.
